VERBATIM COPY of the uncommitted 58-line crates/scriptbots-app/tests/tournament.rs as it stood on 2026-07-25, preserved so the two Elo test bodies cannot be lost to a checkout or stash.

```rust
//! Integration tests for scriptbots-app tournament harness.

use scriptbots_app::tournament::{EloRating, FamilyScore, MatchResult, TournamentHarness};
use std::collections::HashMap;

#[test]
fn test_tournament_integration_elo_progression() {
    let mut harness = TournamentHarness::new();
    harness.register_family("mlp");
    harness.register_family("dwraon");
    harness.register_family("assembly");

    let mut scores1 = HashMap::new();
    scores1.insert(
        "mlp".to_string(),
        FamilyScore {
            survival_share: 0.8,
            biomass_share: 0.7,
            max_generation: 20,
        },
    );
    scores1.insert(
        "dwraon".to_string(),
        FamilyScore {
            survival_share: 0.2,
            biomass_share: 0.3,
            max_generation: 10,
        },
    );

    harness.record_match(MatchResult {
        seed: 100,
        ticks: 1000,
        family_scores: scores1,
    });

    let mlp_rating = harness.ratings.get("mlp").expect("mlp rating");
    let dwraon_rating = harness.ratings.get("dwraon").expect("dwraon rating");

    assert!(mlp_rating.rating > 1500.0);
    assert!(dwraon_rating.rating < 1500.0);
    assert_eq!(mlp_rating.wins, 1);
    assert_eq!(dwraon_rating.wins, 0);

    let leaderboard = harness.generate_leaderboard_markdown();
    assert!(leaderboard.contains("mlp"));
    assert!(leaderboard.contains("dwraon"));
    assert!(leaderboard.contains("assembly"));
}

#[test]
fn test_elo_update_symmetry() {
    let mut r1 = EloRating::new("f1");
    let mut r2 = EloRating::new("f2");
    EloRating::update_elo(&mut r1, &mut r2, 32.0);
    assert!((r1.rating - 1516.0).abs() < 1e-4);
    assert!((r2.rating - 1484.0).abs() < 1e-4);
}
```

description:
Found while surveying HUD layout for bd-v9cz. crates/scriptbots-render/src/lib.rs:10149-10151:

  // Update perf overlay at a modest cadence to reduce churn
  if perf_snapshot.sample_count.is_multiple_of(4) {
      content = content.child(self.render_perf_overlay(perf_snapshot));
  }

GPUI rebuilds the element tree on every render. Gating the .child() call therefore does not throttle the panel's DATA - it throttles the panel's EXISTENCE. The perf overlay is present on one frame in four and absent on the other three, i.e. it strobes at a quarter of frame rate.

The comment shows the intent was to reduce update churn. The correct form keeps the panel mounted unconditionally and throttles the VALUE it displays - hold the last sampled PerfSnapshot in self (self.last_perf already exists and is already assigned two lines above at 10143) and render from that every frame, refreshing the stored sample every 4th.

Roughly:
  self.last_perf = perf_snapshot;            // already present
  content = content.child(self.render_perf_overlay(self.last_perf));   // unconditional

Related to bd-v9cz (HUD layout policy) but independent of it and independently fixable: this is wrong regardless of where the panel ends up living. Render domain - not claiming it, flagging it.
